      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Address Normalization Pipeline",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Address Normalization Pipeline",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "nbSu9U6b_9I5f7sH8noMx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2111.1128525081754,
      "y": 1399.7842980404328,
      "width": 1346.758544921875,
      "height": 375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1363292730,
      "version": 1177,
      "versionNonce": 1818436902,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786385357240,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Stage 1 : Clean -> we remove the noise from the text > trim, lowercase, remove punctuation, collapse whitespace, normalize unicode\nStage 2 : Tokenization -> we normalize the vocabulary ie; Apartment, Apt, Flat, Fl, Unit They all means the same thing\nStage 3 : Entity Extraction ->  using regrex we extract the entities one by one ie; (?i)(flat|apt|apartment|unit)\\s*(no\\.?)?\\s*([a-z]?\\d+)\nStage 4 : Candidate Generation -> we use the lang/long or the pincode to find the societies in that location then we match it with name\n    maybe use the geoIndex db for fast look up so we don't have to run the remaning operation on all the flats in the society\n    we also use Levenshtein distance to match the society names instead of string compare\nStage 5 : Machine learning can entered here to compare scores of each result\n\n\n\nWe basically end up with 3 states\n\n1. Match -> send notification to the user\n2. Ambiguity -> Let the user handle it manually when the rider reaches the society though normal approaval flow\n3. Unknown -> similar to ambiguity",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Stage 1 : Clean -> we remove the noise from the text > trim, lowercase, remove punctuation, collapse whitespace, normalize unicode\nStage 2 : Tokenization -> we normalize the vocabulary ie; Apartment, Apt, Flat, Fl, Unit They all means the same thing\nStage 3 : Entity Extraction ->  using regrex we extract the entities one by one ie; (?i)(flat|apt|apartment|unit)\\s*(no\\.?)?\\s*([a-z]?\\d+)\nStage 4 : Candidate Generation -> we use the lang/long or the pincode to find the societies in that location then we match it with name\n    maybe use the geoIndex db for fast look up so we don't have to run the remaning operation on all the flats in the society\n    we also use Levenshtein distance to match the society names instead of string compare\nStage 5 : Machine learning can entered here to compare scores of each result\n\n\n\nWe basically end up with 3 states\n\n1. Match -> send notification to the user\n2. Ambiguity -> Let the user handle it manually when the rider reaches the society though normal approaval flow\n3. Unknown -> similar to ambiguity",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "qs1QRVGNAFKGaYIq5Gv-F",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3594.244165639488,
      "y": 1402.006520262655,
      "width": 406.99945068359375,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
